WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:03.320
Boxer shorts were introduced in the 1920s

00:00:03.320 --> 00:00:05.730
for, well, boxers.

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:07.910
This underwear was loose around the legs,

00:00:07.910 --> 00:00:10.400
giving boxers the freedom that they needed

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:11.960
to move around the ring.

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:13.350
Then, about a decade later,

00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:14.790
briefs came into the world,

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:17.500
offering a sleeker, tighter-fitting option

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:20.180
and sparking a now-classic question.

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:22.400
Boxers or briefs?

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:26.543
And as it turns out, there may
be a clear winner after all.

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:29.773
You heard that right,

00:00:29.773 --> 00:00:33.280
wearing tight underwear
can lower your sperm count.

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:35.300
Turns out if underwear is too tight,

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:37.890
it pushes the testicles
closer to the body,

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:40.930
increasing their
temperature in the process,

00:00:40.930 --> 00:00:43.750
and that's bad news for the sperm inside.

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:46.420
You see, a man's sperm
production is at its best

00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:48.050
when his testicles are cooler

00:00:48.050 --> 00:00:49.980
than his core body temperature.

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:53.300
Two to 4 degrees Celsius
cooler, to be exact.

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:55.570
That's why the testes hang down

00:00:55.570 --> 00:00:56.910
away from the body

00:00:56.910 --> 00:00:58.680
for most mammals.

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:00.490
So when you wear tight underwear,

00:01:00.490 --> 00:01:03.940
the resulting increase in
temperature can damage the sperm

00:01:03.940 --> 00:01:06.860
and potentially your fertility as well.

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:09.090
Scientists have been studying the link

00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:12.090
between body heat and fertility for years.

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:15.600
Several studies show that men
who work under hot conditions,

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:18.230
like bakers and ceramic oven operators,

00:01:18.230 --> 00:01:20.470
are more likely to have fertility issues

00:01:20.470 --> 00:01:23.250
than men who work cooler jobs.

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:24.670
But ovens, of course,

00:01:24.670 --> 00:01:27.790
are much, much warmer than the human body.

00:01:27.790 --> 00:01:29.100
So it wasn't until recently

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:31.110
that researchers discovered that, yes,

00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:33.650
even small increases in temperature

00:01:33.650 --> 00:01:36.970
from wearing tight underwear
can cause problems.

00:01:36.970 --> 00:01:39.560
In 2018, Harvard researchers released

00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:42.300
the largest study on the subject to date.

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:45.400
They analyzed 656 men

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:47.520
seeking treatment at fertility centers

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:50.150
and recorded their daily
underwear preference,

00:01:50.150 --> 00:01:54.780
boxers or nonboxers,
like briefs and Jockeys.

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:59.550
Sure enough, men who wore boxers
had 33% more mobile sperm.

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:01.290
You know, the kind that can swim

00:02:01.290 --> 00:02:03.150
and successfully fertilize an egg.

00:02:03.150 --> 00:02:05.590
They also just had more sperm in general,

00:02:05.590 --> 00:02:09.790
about 25% more in their collected samples.

00:02:09.790 --> 00:02:12.930
But researchers also found
something they weren't expecting.

00:02:12.930 --> 00:02:15.580
Men in the nonboxers
group had higher levels

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:20.580
of something called a
follicle-stimulating hormone, or FSH.

00:02:20.750 --> 00:02:23.520
FSH is released by the pituitary gland

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:26.520
to help boost sperm
production in the testes.

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:30.290
So researchers think that
an increase in FSH levels

00:02:30.290 --> 00:02:32.420
could be the body's way of compensating

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:34.100
for low sperm production.

00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:35.520
And while both groups of men

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:38.670
still had plenty of sperm
needed to conceive a child,

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:40.630
researchers found that tight underwear

00:02:40.630 --> 00:02:42.700
could jeopardize the fertility of men

00:02:42.700 --> 00:02:45.920
who already suffer from low sperm counts.

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:47.960
Luckily, young, healthy men

00:02:47.960 --> 00:02:50.110
tend to produce sperm continuously.

00:02:50.110 --> 00:02:52.530
So it's possible to reverse damage

00:02:52.530 --> 00:02:55.210
caused by wearing tight underwear

00:02:55.210 --> 00:02:59.443
simply by switching to
a less confining option.

